{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund dedicated police teams to tackle men harassing women in public",
        "additional_details": "Women can face repeated catcalling, intimidation and being followed in public, yet these incidents may not receive timely follow-up when there is no immediate physical harm. We believe police need a dedicated process that recognises patterns early, links repeated reports and intervenes before behaviour escalates. A faster specialist response and visible patrols could help prevent harassment from becoming more serious.",
        "background": "We ask the Government to fund dedicated police responses to men harassing women in public, with a simple and fast reporting route, specialist officers, better identification of repeat offenders, and increased visible patrols in areas where women report frequent harassment.",
